# This repository is edited on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and built in WSL.
# Without this, a branch switch silently rewrites shell scripts with CRLF and
# they stop being executable by bash:
#
#   tools/verify_ref_md.sh: line 10: set: -: invalid option
#   line 27: syntax error near unexpected token `$'do\r''
#
# That has already cost one debugging round, and it fails in a way that looks
# like a broken script rather than a line-ending problem. Worse, the script it
# hit was a VERIFICATION step, which then printed nothing at all -- which reads
# exactly like a verification that found nothing wrong.
#
# Scoped deliberately to files this fork adds. A blanket `*.am text eol=lf`
# also renormalises upstream files that are stored with CRLF (for example
# src/RNAxplorer/doc/Makefile.am), which would put whitespace-only noise in the
# diff against upstream on a branch whose whole point is to be reviewable.
tools/*.sh                  text eol=lf
tests/upstream/*.sh         text eol=lf
tests/upstream/*.c          text eol=lf
tests/mfe_engine.ts         text eol=lf
tests/mfe_cuda_guard.ts     text eol=lf
m4/ac_rna_cuda.m4           text eol=lf
src/ViennaRNA/mfe/cuda/*    text eol=lf
